{"chunk_id": "a72c8057dcd7", "text": "As Ravana abducts Sita and carries her away, the aged vulture-king Jatayu awakens and confronts the demon king. Perched above them, Jatayu rebukes Ravana with a long moral warning, invoking dharma and the duties of kings. He reminds Ravana that Sita is the faithful wife of Rama, a righteous ruler whose wrath will be terrible. Jatayu denounces Ravana\u2019s act as shameful, predicting that abducting Sita is like carrying a deadly serpent or wearing the noose of death. Though extremely old, he declares he will fight to protect her out of loyalty to Rama and King Dasaratha. The scene marks the first heroic resistance to the abduction, highlighting dharma, courage, and the coming clash between Ravana and Rama.\nThe aged vulture king Jatayu confronts Ravana, condemns the abduction of Sita, and challenges him to battle to defend Rama\u2019s wife.\nThemes: dharma vs adharma, loyalty to Rama, defense of Sita, righteous counsel, heroic sacrifice", "vector": [-0.01130660530179739, -0.027426250278949738, -0.011575490236282349, 0.008214430883526802, -0.017558177933096886, 0.014963438734412193, -0.030625978484749794, -0.01648263819515705, -0.022545989602804184, -0.023016538470983505, 0.020031917840242386, 0.010923445224761963, 0.012469532899558544, 0.013424073345959187, -0.008543814532458782, -0.004742455668747425, 0.041488923132419586, -0.003747581969946623, 0.026955701410770416, -0.01668430119752884, -0.004013105761259794, -0.008456426672637463, -0.012167037464678288, 0.008301817812025547, -0.02031424641609192, 0.010244511067867279, 0.02175278030335903, -0.037052325904369354, 0.02593393810093403, -0.009612631984055042, -0.01269808504730463, -0.010123512707650661, -0.015460875816643238, -0.016388528048992157, -0.025181060656905174, 0.002974538132548332, -0.004675234202295542, -0.01337701827287674, 0.022545989602804184, 0.003757665166631341, 0.0009032848756760359, -0.004883619956672192, -0.00849003717303276, 0.0007827068329788744, -0.0037543